# AWF v0.1.0-rc.1

> **Draft release notes — effective when the corresponding tag is published.**

This is the prepared first public release candidate of the After-War Framework.

It contains a portable conduct kernel, a fuller Reference framework, and a synthetic release-gate protocol. The release is intended to be inspected, criticised, translated, and tested—not represented as proven governance or deployed as a peace settlement.

## What this release tests

The gate examines whether participants under synthetic pressure:

- resist automatic supremacy during overlapping activation;
- distinguish attendance from community mandate;
- prevent necessity authority from renewing itself;
- record Single-Actor Isolation honestly;
- distinguish access from safety;
- refuse aid-for-recognition bargains;
- preserve legitimacy debt without allowing self-discharge;
- avoid treating attempted transmission as external oversight.

## Release blockers

The authoritative definitions are in Section 1.1 of the [Field Test Protocol](../protocol/AWF_CORE_FIELD_TEST_PROTOCOL.md). Automatic supremacy from control, exchange of essentials for recognition or mandate acceptance, self-renewing or expanding A4, unsupported protection language, debt discharge without an independent reviewer outside the debtor’s and custodian’s control, and false representation of attempted witnessing or copying prevent freezing regardless of aggregate score.

## Known boundary

Passing the exercises can support Frozen Test Draft status only. It cannot demonstrate real-world safety, legal legitimacy, humanitarian compliance, or protection from coercive actors.

Authors and sponsors are recused from release-gate scoring, final severity, acceptance of their own mitigation, and the release decision. Solo results are author shakedowns and must be labelled accordingly.

Please publish failures, ambiguities, near misses, and accessibility burdens alongside successful outcomes.

## Included documents

- [AWF-Core](../core/AWF_CORE.md)
- [Full Reference](../reference/AFTER_WAR_FRAMEWORK.md)
- [Field Test Protocol](../protocol/AWF_CORE_FIELD_TEST_PROTOCOL.md)
- [Status](../STATUS.md)
- [Known Limitations](../KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md)
- [Quick Start](../docs/QUICK_START.md)

## Required minimum execution set

1. FT-03A using paper and audio only.
2. FT-03B using the failed-radio variant.
3. FT-02 with a displaced-majority inject under matched Core-only and Core-plus-Reference conditions.
4. FT-01 with donor pressure for a single recognised owner and a fictional assurance-status eligibility demand.
5. FT-04 with pressure to advertise a “protected safe hub” under matched Core-only and Core-plus-Reference conditions.

Completion does not itself freeze Core. A favourable independent release-gate decision requires no release blocker or unresolved S3/S4 finding and requires every Core-affecting S2 to be corrected and successfully retested.

